#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096583 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096828 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc92044-1eab-5287-b92c-b0f6b9359b85" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Using the Shell Method"}] :question/id #uuid "9d70bf5e-9f4f-5e73-8105-c3273eb9e735" :question/math-academy-id "e-8852" :question/problem "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $y=2x^3-8x^2+8x$ and the $x$-axis. Calculate the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi$ radians about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 8x &= 0 \\\\\n2x(x^{2} - 4x + 4) &= 0 \\\\\n2x(x - 2)^{2} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=0$ and $x=2$. So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2$.\n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= 2π\\int_{a}^{b}xf(x)dx \\\\\n&= 2π\\int_{0}^{2}x(2x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 8x)dx \\\\\n&= 2π\\int_{0}^{2}2x^{4} - 8x^{3} + 8x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= 4π\\int_{0}^{2}x^{4} - 4x^{3} + 4x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.4π(\\frac{x^{5}}{5} - x^{4} + \\frac{4x^{3}}{3})\\right|_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 4π[(\\frac{2^{5}}{5} - 2^{4} + \\frac{4 \\cdot 2^{3}}{3}) - 0] \\\\\n&= 4π[(\\frac{2^{5}}{5} - \\frac{2^{5}}{2} + \\frac{2^{5}}{3}) - 0] \\\\\n&= 4π \\cdot 2^{5}(\\frac{1}{5} - \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3}) \\\\\n&= 4π \\cdot 32(\\frac{1}{5} - \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{64π}{15}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096584 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a610efd-0cc9-5bec-bb60-d731507c845a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid When a Region is Enclosed Between Two Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "b28d5323-bb98-5eb9-b08f-f7ea663498e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8854" :question/problem "Consider the finite region bounded between the curves $y=3x-x^2$ and $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x^2$. Calculate the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi$ radians about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\nf(x)=3x-x^2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2}x^2\n$$\n\nWe start by determining the points where the curves intersect by solving the following equation for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= g(x) \\\\\n3x - x^{2} &= \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} \\\\\n3x - \\frac{3}{2}x^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx - \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} &= 0 \\\\\n2x - x^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx(2 - x) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=0$ and $x=2$. So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2$.\n\nNow, let's draw our usual vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower and upper functions.\n\n![](images/5a/5a9fd40682646575ada14297ef7e1de766852f99dbdab986d5baa1fb5c2feb94.png)\n\nThe vertical arrow\n\n- *enters* the region through the lower function $y=g(x)=\\dfrac12 x^2$, and\n- *leaves* through the upper function $y=f(x)=3x-x^2$.\n\nTherefore, using the shell method, the volume of the solid can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= 2π\\int_{a}^{b}x([upper] - [lower])dx \\\\\n&= 2π\\int_{0}^{2}x([3x - x^{2}] - [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2}])dx \\\\\n&= 2π\\int_{0}^{2}x(3x - \\frac{3}{2}x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= 6π\\int_{0}^{2}x(x - \\frac{1}{2}x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= 6π\\int_{0}^{2}x(\\frac{2x}{2} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= 3π\\int_{0}^{2}x(2x - x^{2})dx \\\\\n&= 3π\\int_{0}^{2}(2x^{2} - x^{3})dx \\\\\n&= \\left.3π(\\frac{2x^{3}}{3} - \\frac{x^{4}}{4})\\right|_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3π[(\\frac{16}{3} - \\frac{16}{4}) - 0] \\\\\n&= 4π\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097106 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a610efd-0cc9-5bec-bb60-d731507c845a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid When a Region is Enclosed Between Two Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab2358e0-b0f2-59ec-84db-2d50af0e4377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094610} {:answer/id #uuid "b83ed81e-4c22-542b-a341-45e792fe83f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094611} {:answer/id #uuid "df739ef0-1419-5256-ae7d-25c929ecde8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094612} {:answer/id #uuid "3f764d03-00d6-5a11-a3b2-1f362a89340b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094613} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae28776-2bed-5ce9-9290-a8b44b28d5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32π" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094614}] :answer-field/id #uuid "45d1f004-828d-5d62-932b-959a70b00f4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094609}] :question/id #uuid "e4cf3168-db28-57ab-9733-9a47f7b36ec6" :question/math-academy-id "q-139282" :question/problem "Consider the finite region bounded between the curves $y = 2x - \\frac{x^{2}}{2}$ and $y =-x + \\frac{5}{2}$. Calculate the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2π$ radians about the $y$-axis."}]}
